# Generated at runtime: every session key this CSMS has ever minted (AES/HMAC keys in
# the clear). Bench-only material, but it is a per-deployment runtime artifact, not
# something to version - regenerated automatically on first GetEncKey after a restart.
kvas_keys.json

# relay.py's manual exchange log (plan §5.8, D7). bkey is redacted before any line is
# written, but the rest of the wire traffic (sid/cid/tsdt/keyId/battery data) isn't
# something to keep in git history either.
keco_exchange.log

# D8/§3.6/§7: test-only charger PRIVATE keys for shadow-decrypt. This directory must
# only ever hold KECO's openly-published test material (ME12345601's key today) -
# never a real charger's key, which should never exist off that charger's own
# hardware in the first place. Gitignored anyway, defense in depth: nothing here is
# meant to be a durable, version-controlled artifact.
test_only_charger_privkeys/
